        "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >The Game</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fragment is a story-by-metaphor light-horror game that tenderly ventures around deep topics including generational trauma, substance abuse, and depression. You unfold <strong><i>the</i></strong> story by searching for<strong> </strong>good and<strong> </strong>bad memories in a given chapter in the<strong> '<i>loop</i></strong>'. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >The Gameplay</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your memory is fading, things that were once clear are becoming harder and harder to perceive, move fast to process your past or the decay <i><strong>will</strong></i> destroy your memory and take you along with it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Some memories are good, find them and cherish them... or <i><strong>consume</strong></i> them to push the encroaching darkness away.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Some memories are bad, sooner or later we must all come to terms with our trauma and regrets, so that we can close one chapter and move on to the next.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are 3 chapters Fragment (youth, adulthood, old age) each with two environment variations that impact the story. The amount of good memories you hold coming out of one chapter will decide which chapter you enter next, so use them wisely.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game provides the fragments, the rest is up to you... will <i><strong>you</strong></i> break the loop?</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >The Game</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fragment is a story-by-metaphor light-horror game that tenderly ventures around deep topics including generational trauma, substance abuse, and depression. You unfold <strong><i>the</i></strong> story by searching for<strong> </strong>good and<strong> </strong>bad memories in a given chapter in the<strong> '<i>loop</i></strong>'. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >The Gameplay</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Your memory is fading, things that were once clear are becoming harder and harder to perceive, move fast to process your past or the decay <i><strong>will</strong></i> destroy your memory and take you along with it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Some memories are good, find them and cherish them... or <i><strong>consume</strong></i> them to push the encroaching darkness away.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Some memories are bad, sooner or later we must all come to terms with our trauma and regrets, so that we can close one chapter and move on to the next.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are 3 chapters Fragment (youth, adulthood, old age) each with two environment variations that impact the story. The amount of good memories you hold coming out of one chapter will decide which chapter you enter next, so use them wisely.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game provides the fragments, the rest is up to you... will <i><strong>you</strong></i> break the loop?</p>",
